+      "code": "package net.terminalvalue.crosscut.ratelimit;\n\n/**\n * A sliding-window request counter, the rate limit that does not let a client spend two limits at a window\n * boundary: how many requests a client has made in the window its last request fell in, and how many in the window\n * before it, with windows of one length aligned to the epoch (Spring Cloud Gateway's rate limiter keeps such a\n * count per key and window; Resilience4j's {@code RateLimiter} calls the window a cycle). The counter is a value:\n * the filter keeps one per client, replaces it on each request with what {@link #counted} returns, and refuses the\n * request when {@link #estimated} passes the limit. The clock reading and the window length are arguments, so that\n * the counter is a pure function.\n *\n * <p>A counter starts as {@code new Window(0, 0, 0)}: no request yet, in the window at the epoch.\n */\npublic record Window(long startNanos, long count, long previousCount) {\n\n    public Window {\n        if (startNanos < 0 || count < 0 || previousCount < 0) {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"the start and the counts must not be negative\");\n        }\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * The counter after a request at {@code nowNanos}, with windows of {@code windowNanos}: one more in the same\n     * window, or the first request of the next window, with this window's count as the previous count.\n     */\n    public Window counted(long nowNanos, long windowNanos) {\n        if (windowNanos <= 0 || nowNanos < startNanos) {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"the window must be positive and time must not go back\");\n        }\n        if (nowNanos - startNanos < windowNanos) {\n            return new Window(startNanos, count + 1, previousCount);\n        }\n        return new Window(startNanos + windowNanos, 1, count);\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * The requests in the window of {@code windowNanos} ending at {@code nowNanos}, estimated as the current\n     * window's count plus the previous window's count weighted by how much of that sliding window it covers\n     * (the approximation Cloudflare's rate limiter uses).\n     */\n    public long estimated(long nowNanos, long windowNanos) {\n        if (windowNanos <= 0 || nowNanos < startNanos) {\n            throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"the window must be positive and time must not go back\");\n        }\n        long elapsed = Math.min(windowNanos, nowNanos - startNanos);\n        return count + previousCount * (windowNanos - elapsed) / windowNanos;\n    }\n}\n"
